 "what": "a row with a line in the corpus lane's row entries ledger carries, in the facts slot (slot 10, an object), n: the Strong's numbers of the entries its own source files it under, where it has any; t: for a row of a source whose entries are STEP's own tags, those that carry STEP's letter; b: for a row of a source that names BDB's own entries, those entries. A row whose same-source twin under a key ending in a maqaf was struck carries, after its own, the entries of that twin's line that it lacked (followed.entries_given_to_a_twin names each pair). The texts are the served bytes, unchanged. At a place the gate reads these against the tag of the word's core piece",
